# This script is used to create simulation runs of the IHab/HALO Gateway
# environment using the Biosim configuration files generated by TRACLabs.
# With the reduced subset of anomaly scenarios being modeled, the script
# then looks to perform parameter learning to inform the probabilities
# within the Bayesian network CPDs.

# Updated anomaly list to include relevant subgroups and "Unknown Anomaly", and updated anomalies
# with symptoms in both modules to measure whether the hatch between the modules is open (1, True)
# or closed (False, 0)
# Supports running multiple config files in a given run
# Parameter learning mechanism updated to Bayesian Estimation using Dirichlet priors
# (seeking to resolve uniform distributions issue observed using Expectation Maximization)
# Able to perform parameter learning in parallel to reduce training time
# Updated to only perform parameter learning on a subset of the nodes in the network (excluding
# group-level and unknown anomaly nodes, which are predefined and deterministic)
# Also updated 'Hatch Status' to more accurately-defined 'Fan Status' (1='on', 0='off'), that is
# now a parent of module-specific parameters

# Updated on 07/09/2026 to reflect changes to group names and run with connections between parameters
# and group (now subsystem) nodes
# Updated on 08/26/2026 to reflect new updates to subsystem/anomaly/hidden node names
# Updated on 09/01/2026 to finalize changes to new anomaly scenario architecture

# Usage:
#   python learn_probabilities_threaded.py # default: 4 workers, 1000 ticks
#   python learn_probabilities_threaded.py --workers 14 --ticks 500 
#   python learn_probabilities_threaded.py --testing # run full testing across different threads and ticks

